# State carries every attribute of every resource, including the public
# key and the addresses, and a plan file carries the same. Neither is a
# build artifact and neither belongs in a repository that is published.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log

# lab.sh pins host keys here; the addresses change every run.
.known_hosts

# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. It pins the provider
# to the build that was actually run, which is the same promise go.sum
# makes about this repository's one dependency.

# *.tfvars and *.tfvars.json are ignored tree-wide by the repository
# root .gitignore, which says why. They are deliberately not repeated
# here: two copies of one rule drift, and the copy that matters is the
# one covering the directories nobody has created yet.
